1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,860
Your coding interview is recording

2
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:02,700
more than your code.

3
00:00:02,890 --> 00:00:04,030
So when someone pastes

4
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:05,640
an answer from ChatGPT,

5
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:06,690
how do companies

6
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:07,560
actually catch it?

7
00:00:07,770 --> 00:00:08,930
First, the paste.

8
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:10,670
Platforms like HackerRank log

9
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:11,610
every paste and every

10
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:12,670
time you switch tabs.

11
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,230
Forty clean lines appearing

12
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,100
in one frame is

13
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:16,220
not how humans type.

14
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:17,650
Next, your typing rhythm.

15
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,170
Real coders type, pause,

16
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:20,090
delete and fix.

17
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:21,280
AI answers show

18
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:21,980
a long pause,

19
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:22,880
then a sudden burst

20
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:23,800
of perfect code.

21
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:25,920
HackerRank's model even flags deleting

22
00:00:25,770 --> 00:00:27,290
a big block and retyping

23
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:28,440
it in an odd rhythm.

24
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:29,780
Then, the comparison.

25
00:00:29,910 --> 00:00:31,620
CodeSignal checks your answer against

26
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:33,150
every submission on its platform

27
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,690
and solutions posted online,

28
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:35,650
and rolls it all

29
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:36,930
into one suspicion score.

30
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:38,300
A human reviewer still

31
00:00:38,150 --> 00:00:39,120
makes the final call.

32
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:40,490
And it's rising.

33
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:42,340
CodeSignal says cheating attempts

34
00:00:42,190 --> 00:00:43,740
jumped from 16% to

35
00:00:43,590 --> 00:00:45,270
35% in one year.

36
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:47,060
But what about live interviews,

37
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:48,290
where the AI hides in

38
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:49,590
an invisible overlay that

39
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:50,810
screen share never sees?

40
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:52,630
That's where humans take over.

41
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:54,260
Interviewers watch your eyes drift

42
00:00:54,110 --> 00:00:55,100
to the same spot,

43
00:00:54,950 --> 00:00:56,100
the glow in your glasses,

44
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:57,060
and the long hmm

45
00:00:56,910 --> 00:00:58,190
while the answer loads.

46
00:00:58,270 --> 00:00:59,190
In one survey,

47
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:01,070
81% of Big Tech interviewers

48
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:02,610
had suspected AI cheating,

49
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:04,570
and 31% had caught someone.

50
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:05,940
Their best trick is simple.

51
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:07,350
One follow-up question.

52
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,540
Why this approach?

53
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:09,470
What breaks if

54
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:10,490
the input doubles?

55
00:01:10,630 --> 00:01:12,000
The AI wrote the code,

56
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:13,150
but it can't explain it

57
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,260
for you in real time.

58
00:01:14,110 --> 00:01:15,620
That's why Google brought

59
00:01:15,470 --> 00:01:16,840
back an in-person round,

60
00:01:17,030 --> 00:01:18,790
and Amazon asks candidates to

61
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:20,190
promise they won't use AI.

62
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:21,700
So use AI to prepare,

63
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:22,520
not to perform.

64
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:23,550
Think out loud,

65
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:24,720
even when you're stuck.

66
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:25,870
Follow for more breakdowns,

67
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:26,610
and send this to the

68
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:28,300
friend who keeps ChatGPT open

69
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:29,100
in the other tab.

